<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Oaxaca state '96 lumber sales increase.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Oaxaca state '96 lumber sales increase.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's southern state of Oaxaca sold 505,000 cubic meters of lumber in 1996, up 84,000 cubic meters from sales recorded a year earlier, the state-owned news agency Notimex said Monday.</p>
<p>Citing Oaxaca state farm and forest director Adolfo Toledo Infanzon, Notimex said for 1997 the state plans to boost output and sales, especially of high-price paying varieties.</p>
<p>Oaxaca is one of Mexico's secondary lumber producing states, behind more northerly states such as Durango and Chihuahua which have significant output and sales.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
